  },
  {
   "id": "h185",
   "kind": "html",
   "en": "<span class=\"skill-n\">02</span><span class=\"skill-gain\">+20–40 s</span>"
  },
  {
   "id": "h186",
   "kind": "html",
   "en": "Iso Wall Sit"
  },
  {
   "id": "h187",
   "kind": "html",
   "en": "Leg strength-endurance"
  },
  {
   "id": "h188",
   "kind": "html",
   "en": "Wk 1"
  },
  {
   "id": "h189",
   "kind": "html",
   "en": "Wk 8"
  },
  {
   "id": "h190",
   "kind": "html",
   "en": "<span class=\"skill-n\">03</span><span class=\"skill-gain\">+10–20 s</span>"
  },
  {
   "id": "h191",
   "kind": "html",
   "en": "Copenhagen Plank — Long"
  },
  {
   "id": "h192",
   "kind": "html",
   "en": "Groin durability"
  },
  {
   "id": "h193",
   "kind": "html",
   "en": "Wk 1"
  },
  {
   "id": "h194",
   "kind": "html",
   "en": "Wk 8"
  },
  {
   "id": "h195",
   "kind": "html",
   "en": "<span class=\"skill-n\">04</span><span class=\"skill-gain\">+15–30 s</span>"
  },
  {
   "id": "h196",
   "kind": "html",
   "en": "Hanging / Bar Hold"
  },
  {
   "id": "h197",
   "kind": "html",
   "en": "Grip &amp; upper-body endurance"
  },
  {
   "id": "h198",
   "kind": "html",
   "en": "Wk 1"
  },
  {
   "id": "h199",
   "kind": "html",
   "en": "Wk 8"
  },
  {
   "id": "h200",
   "kind": "html",
   "en": "<span class=\"skill-n\">05</span><span class=\"skill-gain\">+1–2 levels</span>"
  },
  {
   "id": "h201",
   "kind": "html",
   "en": "Beep Test"
  },
  {
   "id": "h202",
   "kind": "html",
   "en": "Aerobic engine (VO2max)"
  },
  {
   "id": "h203",
   "kind": "html",
   "en": "Wk 1"
  },
  {
   "id": "h204",
   "kind": "html",
   "en": "Wk 8"
  },
  {
   "id": "h205",
   "kind": "html",
   "en": "Still fast.<br>Still here."
  },
  {
   "id": "h206",
   "kind": "html",
   "en": "Re-test every few weeks and watch the numbers hold or climb — that's a body staying in the game."
  },
  {
   "id": "h207",
   "kind": "html",
   "en": "06 — Players"
  },
  {
   "id": "h208",
   "kind": "html",
   "en": "Trusted by veteran <em>players.</em>"
  },
  {
   "id": "h209",
   "kind": "html",
   "en": "From players who plan to keep lacing up for years — and wanted off-ice training that respects a 40+ body."
  },
  {
   "id": "h210",
   "kind": "html",
   "en": "47 and I just had my best season in a decade. My groin held all year and my first step is back. The Mon/Wed/Fri spacing is the part I didn't know I needed."
  },
  {
   "id": "h211",
   "kind": "html",
   "en": "S"
  },
  {
   "id": "h212",
   "kind": "html",
   "en": "Steve W."
  },
  {
   "id": "h213",
   "kind": "html",
   "en": "Beer-league · age 47"
  },
  {
   "id": "h214",
   "kind": "html",
   "en": "Finally a program that doesn't pretend I'm 25. Joint-friendly, band-based, and I'm not wrecked the next morning. My balance and single-leg strength are night and day."
  },
  {
   "id": "h215",
   "kind": "html",
   "en": "R"
  },
  {
   "id": "h216",
   "kind": "html",
   "en": "Rob M."
  },
  {
   "id": "h217",
   "kind": "html",
   "en": "Rec-league player"
  },
  {
   "id": "h218",
   "kind": "html",
   "en": "I do it in the basement with one band. Fewer aches, and I'm noticeably quicker on my edges. Worth it just to keep playing pain-free for years to come."
  },
  {
   "id": "h219",
   "kind": "html",
   "en": "G"
  },
  {
   "id": "h220",
   "kind": "html",
   "en": "Greg H."
  },
  {
   "id": "h221",
   "kind": "html",
   "en": "Old-timers league"
  },
  {
   "id": "h222",
   "kind": "html",
   "en": "07 — The Kit"
  },
  {
   "id": "h223",
   "kind": "html",
   "en": "No gym. <em>No pounding.</em>"
  },
  {
   "id": "h224",
   "kind": "html",
   "en": "Almost zero equipment, and deliberately joint-friendly. For a 40+ body, bands and bodyweight done with quality are exactly right — a design choice, not a compromise."
  },
  {
   "id": "h225",
   "kind": "html",
   "en": "Loop resistance bands"
  },
  {
   "id": "h226",
   "kind": "html",
   "en": "Light dumbbells (optional)"
  },
  {
   "id": "h227",
   "kind": "html",
   "en": "A low box or bench"
  },
  {
   "id": "h228",
   "kind": "html",
   "en": "Space to move"
  },
  {
   "id": "h229",
   "kind": "html",
   "en": "An open stretch for sprints"
  },
  {
   "id": "h230",
   "kind": "html",
   "en": "The whole program runs on a band and your bodyweight; a light pair of dumbbells is an optional bonus, never required. No barbells, no heavy weights, no gym."
  },
  {
   "id": "h231",
   "kind": "html",
   "en": "08 — Built to Last"
  },
  {
   "id": "h232",
   "kind": "html",
   "en": "Train <em>smart.</em>"
  },
  {
   "id": "h233",
   "kind": "html",
   "en": "<b>Recovery decides.</b> After 40, recovery and tissue tolerance — not work capacity — decide what you can train. Every session is dosed to make you better without beating you up."
  },
  {
   "id": "h234",
   "kind": "html",
   "en": "<b>Durability first.</b> Joint prep, soft landings, and a full rest day between every session are non-negotiable. We build the player who's still fast at 45 — not the one who's hurt by week three."
  },
  {
   "id": "h235",
   "kind": "html",
   "en": "09 — Questions"
  },
  {
   "id": "h236",
   "kind": "html",
   "en": "Good to <em>know.</em>"
  },
  {
   "id": "h237",
   "kind": "html",
   "en": "<span>I've got some aches — is this safe at 40+?</span><span class=\"faq-ico\"></span>"
  },
  {
   "id": "h238",
   "kind": "html",
   "en": "It's built for exactly that. Durability-first: joint prep, soft landings, band and bodyweight loading (light dumbbells optional), and a full rest day between sessions, with easier scaling on everything. As always, get a pre-participation check from your doctor — especially with any heart condition or ongoing joint pain."
  },
  {
   "id": "h239",
   "kind": "html",
   "en": "<span>Do I need a gym or weights?</span><span class=\"faq-ico\"></span>"
  },
  {
   "id": "h240",
   "kind": "html",
   "en": "No. Bands and your bodyweight run the whole program (light dumbbells optional) — no barbells, no gym, all doable at home. The sprint tests just need a longer open stretch."
  },
  {
   "id": "h241",
   "kind": "html",
   "en": "<span>How is the program delivered?</span><span class=\"faq-ico\"></span>"
  },
  {
   "id": "h242",
   "kind": "html",
   "en": "It's a clean, interactive web program you open on any phone, tablet, or laptop — with a demo video built into every exercise. No PDF to lose, no app to install. Buy once and it's yours forever."
  },
  {
   "id": "h243",
   "kind": "html",
   "en": "<span>How much time does each session take?</span><span class=\"faq-ico\"></span>"
  },
  {
   "id": "h244",
   "kind": "html",
   "en": "About 50–70 minutes, three times a week — Monday, Wednesday, Friday, with a full rest day between. That spacing is part of the program: after 40, tendons need it. If the week gets squeezed, drop a session rather than doubling up."
  },
  {
   "id": "h245",
   "kind": "html",
   "en": "<span>Will it really make a difference at my age?</span><span class=\"faq-ico\"></span>"
  },
  {
   "id": "h246",
   "kind": "html",
   "en": "Yes — you'll land cleaner, balance better, accelerate harder, and feel more durable, and the five checkpoints prove it. It's not about chasing 20-year-old numbers (that's how veterans get hurt) — it's about staying fast, strong, and on the ice, season after season."
  },
  {
   "id": "h247",
   "kind": "html",
   "en": "<span>Is it too late to start before the season?</span><span class=\"faq-ico\"></span>"
  },
  {
   "id": "h248",
   "kind": "html",
